SQL DROP DATABASE Statement

The SQL DROP DATABASE statement is used to permanently delete an existing SQL database.

Note: Be careful before dropping a database! Dropping a database deletes the database and all its content (tables, views, stored procedures, and data).

Syntax
DROP DATABASE database_name;

MySQL Syntax
DROP DATABASE database_name;

SQL Server Syntax
DROP DATABASE database_name;

DROP DATABASE Example
The following SQL statement drops an existing database named "testDB":

Example:
DROP DATABASE testDB;

Detailed Notes
- `DROP DATABASE` removes the entire database and all objects inside it.
- This operation is irreversible in most systems unless you have a backup.
- Administrative privileges or database-level permissions are usually required.
- In MySQL, if the database does not exist, the statement will return an error unless you use `DROP DATABASE IF EXISTS database_name;`.
- In SQL Server, you may need to set the database to single-user mode or ensure no active connections before dropping it.
- Always verify the database name before running this command to avoid accidental data loss.

MySQL Example with IF EXISTS:
DROP DATABASE IF EXISTS testDB;

SQL Server Example with single user mode and drop:
ALTER DATABASE testDB SET SINGLE_USER WITH ROLLBACK IMMEDIATE;
DROP DATABASE testDB;

Show Databases After Drop
MySQL:
SHOW DATABASES;

SQL Server:
SELECT name FROM sys.databases;

Common Uses
- Remove a test or development database that is no longer needed.
- Delete a database for a decommissioned application.
- Clear space on the server by removing unused databases.

Warnings
- Do not use `DROP DATABASE` on production databases unless you are certain.
- Back up any important data before executing the command.
- Dropping a database also removes permissions, users, and referenced objects associated with that database.

Exercise Question
What is the purpose of the SQL DROP DATABASE statement?
- To delete an existing database

Incorrect answers:
- To delete a table from a database (wrong)
- To delete all records in a table (wrong)
- To delete specific rows from a database (wrong)
